# BoronDNS RPM package

The RPM installs static MUSL BoronDNS and BoronGun executables, creates the
`borondns` system account, and installs `borondns.service`. The service only
starts after `/etc/borondns-secondary/config.toml` exists.

Configuration and `/var/lib/borondns`, including the zone cache, are retained
when the package is removed. Delete operational data explicitly only when it is
no longer required.

Remove or migrate an archive installation and its locally managed
`/etc/systemd/system/borondns.service` before installing this RPM.
